<title>CHINA: Shenzhen bourse opens new repurchase contracts.</title>
<headline>Shenzhen bourse opens new repurchase contracts.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Shenzhen stock exchange on Thursday opened three-day and four-day repurchase contracts, the first time repo papers of this duration have been traded, the China Securities newspaper said.</p>
<p>This brings the total number of repo papers on the bourse to nine, it said. The exchange also has seven-, 14-, 28-, 63-, 91-, 182- and 273-day repurchase contracts listed.</p>
</text>
